     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum metformin dose. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possible intended doses:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release)\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg or 850 mg PO two or three times daily**, if the patient is starting metformin or being titrated up\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a reason. I can add that to the order note, though I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
